Manage machine

Usage:
  bootwright machine [command]

Available Commands:
  exec        Run a command over SSH as the Machine's resolved identity; confirm or refuse an unproved host key and return the client's exit status
  list        List machines and the lifecycle position each has reached
  restart     Restart one machine through its management controller
  rsh         Open an SSH session as the Machine's resolved identity; confirm or refuse an unproved host key and return the client's exit status
  start       Power one machine on through its management controller
  stop        Shut one machine down through its management controller
  trust       Inspect and maintain exact host-key trust

Global Flags:
      --context string             Select a context (default: current context)
  -h, --help                       Show help for this command
      --ssh-ask-sudo-password      Request the borrowed account's sudo password
      --ssh-id-file string         Offer an explicit private key for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user string            Borrow an explicit POSIX account for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user-for-provisioned   Extend the borrowed account to provisioned machines

Use "bootwright machine [command] --help" for more information about a command.
